course: dictionary
lesson: 10038
title: Termites and their mounds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A termite is a small, pale insect. Termites live together in large groups called colonies, and they eat wood. «Termites are sometimes called white ants but are not ants at all», so the name can fool you.
explain: Look at the words around a new word to find its meaning. «The termites live in the nest underground» tells you where a termite colony lives. A mound is a big heap that termites build as their nest, so a termite mound is a nest that termites have built.
fact: A termite is a small, pale insect that lives in a large group called a colony.
fact: «Termite mound» means a large nest built by termites, and some can be taller than a person.
fact: «Termite damage» means harm done by termites, often when they eat the wood in houses.
fact: Termites are not ants, even though people sometimes call them white ants.
exercise: What is a termite? | A type of stone found in mountains | A large bird that nests in trees | A kind of fish that swims in rivers | *A small, pale insect that lives in large groups and eats wood
exercise: What is a «termite colony»? | A tall tree with green leaves | *A large group of termites living together | A single termite flying alone | A wooden table in a kitchen
exercise: Which word in «Termites are sometimes called white ants but are not ants at all» shows that termites are a different animal from ants? | called | *not | white | sometimes
test: What does «termite damage» mean? | Music played on a drum | *Harm done by termites, often when they eat wood | A sweet smell from a flower | A new kind of paint for walls
test: A «termite mound» is: | A type of cake | A pile of leaves blown by the wind | *A large nest built by termites | A small hill of sand at the beach
exam: Termites eat wood and live in colonies. Which animal is a termite? | A fish with a long tail | A large mammal that lives alone | A plant with green leaves | *A small, pale insect that lives in large groups
